      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Further testing has lead me to understand the audio delay better.\nAudio gets delayed several seconds, sometimes even like a minute. This happens both for my voice as I'm speaking and it getting sent to other players (happens always), as well as for other players' voices when they start breaking up (which happens at around 4 players or so, more in heavier in worlds).\nWhat seems to be happening is that the audio playback gets interrupted for whatever reason and gets stopped for a moment, and then it picks up again at the same point in the audio buffer without skipping any data, causing ever increasing delays. I think that if audio playback gets interrupted for any reason we need to discard data, or at least when the playback pointer is more than a certain amount of seconds away from the point where data is inserted into the audio buffer.\nIt is possible to notice the delay of my own speech in game, as I can observe the lips of my avatar moving long after I stopped speaking (even if I mute directly after finishing speaking).\nSpeaking of muting, it seems that muting myself while not speaking ameloriates the problem with delays slightly. Maybe because it gives the game a point to \"catch up\" at.\nNotably these issues usually occur only with voice, world BGM and avatar sounds usually play back fine without skips (except in certain circumstances when very heavily loaded/heavier worlds). The voice issues happen even while not under particularly heavy load.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
